#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:66
#: 2dfbcb84c572453f9aa9b40495d7146b
msgid ""
"Only after all three layers have been consulted does the system hand "
"candidate pages to Chapter 16's L1/L2/L3 dispatcher. The sync does *not* "
"itself update anything; its job is purely to produce a reviewable, "
"deduplicated, smallest-safe set of candidate pages."
msgstr ""
"只有在三层都被依次咨询过之后，系统才会把候选页面交给第 16 章的 L1/L2/L3 派发器。同步本身 * 不 * "
"修改任何页面；它的职责就是产出一份可评审、已去重、“最小而安全”的候选页面集合。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:71
#: 6b6c3d313c384d46ae272e6a96dc37fd
msgid ""
"This separation — detect candidates here, update them there — is why Chapter"
" 7a's model scales. Detection is cheap and deterministic; update is "
"expensive and sometimes uses an LLM. Combining them into one step couples "
"the two cost models and usually picks the worst of both."
msgstr ""
"这种分离 —— 候选在这里检测、更新在那边做 —— 是第 7a 章那套模型能规模化的原因。检测便宜、确定性强；更新贵，且有时要调 "
"LLM。把两件事并成一步，会把两种成本模型耦合在一起，结果往往是两边的缺点都被占满。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:76
#: c28b590a33f143689e64cb5235189ee8
msgid "How"
msgstr "How —— 怎么做"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:78
#: 4affc42e0b774d46aa87df8057d2ebe6
msgid "The L-git layer"
msgstr "L-git 层"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:80
#: 81c9c2390c934537911174fca3fc86d2
msgid ""
"The cheapest layer. Every page carries a `commit:` field in its footer "
"(Chapter 5 C2). On every sync, the job computes the set of files that have "
"changed between any page's `commit:` and `HEAD`:"
msgstr ""
"最便宜的一层。每个页面都在 footer 中带一个 `commit:` 字段（第 5 章 C2）。在每次同步时，作业会计算“该页面 `commit:` "
"与 `HEAD` 之间发生过变化的文件集合”："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:94
#: edeb085698d241a794d334621cca6e9c
msgid ""
"A page whose footer already points at `HEAD` is skipped entirely — no body "
"read, no LLM invocation. This is the L1-mechanical case in its purest form: "
"the cost of \"this page is fine\" is a git command."
msgstr ""
"footer 已经指向 `HEAD` 的页面会被完全跳过 —— 不读正文、不调 LLM。这就是 L1 机械化场景最纯粹的形态：“这个页面没事”的成本 ="
" 一次 git 命令。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:98
#: a91d27c55b6f4f5798bb847e4823169d
msgid ""
"The footer's `commit:` field is therefore not decorative. It is the load-"
"bearing datum L-git keys on. A KB that drops the field (or lets it fall out "
"of sync because review happens without updating it) loses L-git and falls "
"back to L-entity and L-link, which are both more expensive."
msgstr ""
"所以 footer 里的 `commit:` 字段不是装饰。它是 L-git "
"真正赖以工作的承重数据。一个知识库如果丢掉这个字段（或者因为“评审时只看没写回”让它脱节），就等于丢掉了 L-git，从此只能落到 L-entity 和"
" L-link —— 这两层都要贵得多。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:104
#: 16ddc375e8c341cb9a3ad1553ff8c856
msgid "The L-entity layer"
msgstr "L-entity 层"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:106
#: b370c391d8be47129f040a06ad111721
msgid ""
"L-git only detects *which files* changed. A refactor that renames an "
"exported function does not rename any file — but it does break every page "
"that cited the function by name. L-entity catches these by keying on the "
"code-layer entity IDs defined in Chapter 11."
msgstr ""
"L-git 只能检测到 * 哪些文件 * 变了。一次重命名了导出函数的重构并不会重命名任何文件 —— "
"但它会打破每一个按名字引用该函数的页面。L-entity 正是通过以第 11 章定义的代码层实体 ID 为 key，来捕捉这类情况。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:111
#: 4d6b52db46cf4656ab10e4f0d2e2d940
msgid ""
"Every code entity has a stable ID: `sha256(repoID | filePath | entityType | "
"name | startLine)`. When the code-layer sync runs (Chapter 11), entities "
"whose IDs changed land in a `moved_entities` set. L-entity then asks: *which"
" prose pages cite these entities?* The answer comes from a reverse index "
"built by the verify step (Chapter 7), which scans every page for `file:line`"
" anchors and records a `(page, entity_id)` edge."
msgstr ""
"每个代码实体都有一个稳定 ID：`sha256(repoID | filePath | entityType | name | "
"startLine)`。代码层同步跑完后（第 11 章），ID 发生变化的实体会落入一个 `moved_entities` 集合。L-entity "
"接着问： * 哪些文稿页面引用了这些实体？ * 答案来自 verify 步骤（第 7 章）构建的反向索引 —— 它会扫描每个页面的 "
"`file:line` 锚点，并记录一条 `(page, entity_id)` 边。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:126
#: be34516bfad04a598e5dabbc44a51937
msgid ""
"L-entity is the layer that keeps the *prose layer in sync with the code "
"layer*. Without it, a function-rename refactor leaves the prose citing a "
"dead entity, and a retrieval agent (Chapter 21) cheerfully quotes the dead "
"citation. With it, the page gets flagged, routed through Chapter 16's L2 "
"bounded-LLM path, and re-cited against the current code."
msgstr ""
"L-entity 是让 * 文稿层与代码层保持同步 * 的那一层。没有它，一次重命名函数的重构会让文稿继续引用一个已死的实体，而一个检索 agent（第"
" 21 章）会照样欢快地把这条引用引出来。有了它，页面会被打上标记，走第 16 章的 L2 有界 LLM 路径，重新针对当前代码引用一次。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:133
#: 6976a8ece79b4b0dba6d2659e0a70f52
msgid "The L-link layer"
msgstr "L-link 层"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:135
#: a60ee3422dcc470fa18c7d063a822944
msgid ""
"Catches everything the first two layers miss: a reordered section in another"
" page that shifts `ch05-frontmatter#foo` anchors; a moved example file that "
"breaks every `literalinclude` path; a deleted image in `_static/`. L-link is"
" a brute-force scan — every outgoing link in every page is tested against "
"the current commit."
msgstr ""
"捕获前两层漏掉的一切：另一页中重排的章节导致 `ch05-frontmatter#foo` 锚点移位；一个被移动的示例文件把每一条 "
"`literalinclude` 路径都打断；`_static/` 中一张被删除的图片。L-link 是暴力扫描 —— 每个页面里的每一个外链都会对当前"
" commit 重新测试一次。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:148
#: a97e9ca70aa5429db6134f8dd85b011f
msgid ""
"L-link can feel expensive, but it is not: the checks are pure filesystem "
"operations and finish in seconds for a 1,000-page KB. It runs in full on "
"every sync — there is no incremental shortcut here, because a link can break"
" due to a change in the *target*, which L-git and L-entity already knew "
"about, but also because of a change in the *source* that neither layer saw "
"(e.g. a page edited manually in `vim`)."
msgstr ""
"L-link 看起来贵，其实不贵：这些检查都是纯文件系统操作，对 1000 个页面的知识库而言会在数秒内完成。它在每次同步时都整体跑一遍 —— "
"这里没有增量捷径，因为一条链接可能因 * 目标 * 的变更而断（L-git 和 L-entity 已经知道这类变更），也可能因为 * 源 * "
"的变更而断，而后者这两层谁都没看到（例如有人直接用 `vim` 改了一个页面）。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:156
#: 548e5457531c4b67a72c00f2ce1bcdee
msgid "Producing the candidate set"
msgstr "产出候选集合"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:158
#: afaef7c3c8e14548afa93266ed260e92
msgid ""
"The three layers emit candidate pages with some overlap. The sync "
"deduplicates and tags each candidate with the layer(s) that caught it, so "
"Chapter 16's dispatcher can use that tag to choose a level:"
msgstr "三层发射出来的候选页面会有一定重叠。同步阶段会去重，并给每个候选打上“是哪一层捕获到它的”标签，好让第 16 章的派发器据此选择级别："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: 43c68542045d4246a8296a0567855c80
msgid "Caught by"
msgstr "捕获层"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: add2c7f9412c433ea9a0fe2ea616a589
msgid "Suggested level (Chapter 16)"
msgstr "建议级别（第 16 章）"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: f5e859a5277f43f4b30d9bc57398acdc
msgid "L-git only, and only the footer `commit:` drifted"
msgstr "仅 L-git，且只有 footer 的 `commit:` 发生漂移"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: 22b0ee546431409aa86cca5b2ee45d61
msgid "**L1** re-stamp"
msgstr "**L1** 重打时间戳"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: 0f9a540323ee4bc5bb0208de7acba9d3
msgid "L-git only, and real body-citing files changed"
msgstr "仅 L-git，且真正被正文引用的文件发生了变化"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: e30ba5d0f0e540b3b1768439aac805df
msgid "**L2** bounded-LLM"
msgstr "**L2** 有界 LLM"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: 6b699f0d7492454ea98cb66194346531
msgid "L-entity"
msgstr "L-entity"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: 397778cd58cc43c180d4ef02dbe0dc5a
msgid "**L2** bounded-LLM, with the moved-entity ID in context"
msgstr "**L2** 有界 LLM，并把移动实体的 ID 放进上下文"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: 74f5d88e91c2486b8ce7a5a23b65e1b9
msgid "L-link (target moved)"
msgstr "L-link（目标已移动）"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: 6a96f8913d1e4bc6992ac7afd9e8a283
msgid "**L1** link fix if possible; else **L2**"
msgstr "能修就走 **L1** 链接修复；否则走 **L2**"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: cc65f89df2864926b328c22f996d6834
msgid "Any layer + page is in `architecture/` or `adr/`"
msgstr "任意一层 + 页面位于 `architecture/` 或 `adr/`"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md
#: 435089fe1af0447991a4d217c498001b
msgid "**L3** human-led"
msgstr "**L3** 人工主导"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:170
#: d5a41e768a6e4c0f8811e5eb3bf63b23
msgid ""
"The last row matters. Architecture pages and ADRs are security-sensitive "
"prose; the operational model refuses to let an LLM silently regenerate them "
"regardless of what the earlier layers said. This is a policy, stated once in"
" the dispatcher's config, not re- litigated per page."
msgstr ""
"最后一行很关键。架构页和 ADR 都是安全敏感的文稿；运维模型拒绝让 LLM 在无人知晓的情况下悄悄重新生成它们 —— "
"不管前面几层怎么判。这是一条策略，在派发器配置里只声明一次，而不是在每个页面上反复争论。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:176
#: 3b4781ac6e3f4051b04ea83fe08b1b04
msgid "Example"
msgstr "Example —— 范例"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:178
#: 0ce8e0f981dd47b88a78246d7752168e
msgid ""
"A concrete sync against a PR that renames a Go package from "
"`internal/worker` to `internal/job`:"
msgstr "针对一个把 Go 包从 `internal/worker` 改名为 `internal/job` 的 PR，跑一次具体的同步："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:181
#: a7cfd52e848b4a06a7081898c0129eec
msgid ""
"**Input diff.** 12 files changed. 4 under `internal/worker/` (now "
"`internal/job/`). 8 callers that imported the old package."
msgstr ""
"**输入 diff。** 12 个文件变了。其中 4 个原本在 `internal/worker/`（现在在 `internal/job/`）下；8 "
"个是此前导入旧包的调用方。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:184
#: cf73828df4764069af24b4fd86b19142
msgid ""
"**L-git.** Produces 12 candidate files. Of the pages in the KB, three have "
"`commit:` values predating the PR: `data-and-api.md`, `repo-map.md`, "
"`runbook.md`. All three are added to candidates."
msgstr ""
"**L-git。** 产出 12 个候选文件。在知识库的页面中，有三个的 `commit:` 值落在 PR 之前：`data-and-"
"api.md`、`repo-map.md`、`runbook.md`。三个都被加入候选集。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:188
#: 372c1e5a32094b998df73965d7741c39
msgid ""
"**L-entity.** The code-layer sync reports 9 moved entities (the package's 9 "
"exported symbols kept the same `name` but now live under a different "
"`filePath`, so their stable ID changed). The reverse index shows `data-and-"
"api.md` cites 3 of them and `repo-map.md` cites 1. Both pages were already "
"candidates; L-entity adds nothing new — it does attach the moved-entity IDs "
"so L2 has them in its context."
msgstr ""
"**L-entity。** 代码层同步报告了 9 个移动实体（该包的 9 个导出符号 `name` 保持不变、但 `filePath` "
"变了，所以它们的稳定 ID 也跟着变了）。反向索引显示 `data-and-api.md` 引用了其中 3 个，`repo-map.md` 引用了 1 "
"个。两个页面本来就在候选集里；L-entity 没有新增候选 —— 但它把这些“移动实体 ID”挂上来，好让 L2 在上下文里能拿到。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:195
#: d0e1206e98194c33991a72e9b0ee9dde
msgid ""
"**L-link.** Every `internal/worker/...` literal path in the KB is now "
"broken. `repo-map.md` had 4 such paths; `data-and-api.md` had 2. Both were "
"already candidates."
msgstr ""
"**L-link。** 知识库中所有 `internal/worker/...` 字面路径都已失效。`repo-map.md` 里有 4 "
"条这样的路径；`data-and-api.md` 里有 2 条。两个页面也都已经在候选集里。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:199
#: bca7fb5a9d6344af86fa587a132b3253
msgid ""
"**Dispatcher input.** Three candidates, all tagged with the layer(s) that "
"caught them:"
msgstr "**派发器输入。** 三个候选页面，每个都带着“是哪一层抓到它的”标签："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:208
#: 56aa60ea7b674b21a3479daea006641e
msgid ""
"Chapter 16 takes it from here: L1 regenerates `repo-map.md` from `git ls-"
"files` in zero tokens; L2 invokes an LLM on `data-and-api.md` with the "
"moved-entity diff and the existing body; L1 re-stamps `runbook.md`'s footer."
" Total cost: one LLM call, ~3 kB of context, under a cent. Human review "
"scope: one diff (`data-and-api.md`). Compare with a naive \"re-embed "
"everything\" baseline that would have produced diffs across dozens of pages "
"for the reviewer to wade through."
msgstr ""
"接力棒交到第 16 章：L1 用 `git ls-files` 以零 token 重新生成 `repo-map.md`；L2 拿着“移动实体 diff "
"+ 现有正文”对 `data-and-api.md` 调一次 LLM；L1 给 `runbook.md` 的 footer 重打一次时间戳。总成本：一次"
" LLM 调用，约 3 kB 上下文，不到一美分。人工评审范围：一份 diff（`data-and-"
"api.md`）。对比一下朴素的“全部重嵌入”基线：那种做法会让评审者在几十个页面的 diff 里蹚来蹚去。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:216
#: d31a9d8e67d84534b0af334141496ed6
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "Conclusion —— 小结"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:218
#: 026a103d07fc4f49ab17c76778174f00
msgid ""
"Incremental sync is the interface between the code layer (Part III) and the "
"prose layer (Part II). Everything upstream of it is about *correctness* — "
"\"does this entity ID still point at the same thing?\", \"does this link "
"resolve?\" — and everything downstream is about *cost* — \"is this a free "
"re-stamp, a cheap regeneration, or a human's problem?\" Get the interface "
"right and both halves of the book's model work. Get it wrong and the cheap "
"layers end up doing expensive work."
msgstr ""
"增量同步是代码层（第三部分）与文稿层（第二部分）之间的接口。它上游的所有东西都在谈 * 正确性 * ——“这个实体 ID "
"是否仍然指向同一件事？”“这个链接是否还能解析？”；它下游的所有东西都在谈 * 成本 * "
"——“这是一次免费的重打时间戳、一次便宜的重生成，还是必须交给人？”把这道接口做对，本书模型的两半就都能跑起来；做错了，便宜的层就会被迫干贵的活。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:226
#: b25bfd0539ac44c7a498f024575d8047
msgid ""
"The next chapter makes the gates explicit: a page that has been processed by"
" any update level still has to pass the same hard checks (footer present, "
"references resolve, no broken Mermaid) before it can be published. Detection"
" and dispatch are ch14 and ch16; gating is ch15."
msgstr ""
"下一章会把各种门禁显式讲清楚：不管一个页面被哪一种更新级别处理过，它在发布前依然要通过同一套硬性检查（footer 存在、引用能解析、没有坏掉的 "
"Mermaid）。检测与派发是第 14、16 章的事；门禁则属于第 15 章。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch14-incremental-sync.md:232
#: 4877bc5e8fd444d9859c25d902988c25
msgid "References"
msgstr "参考文献"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "for each page P in content/**/*.md:\n"
#~ "    prev := P.footer.commit\n"
#~ "    changed := `git diff --name-only prev..HEAD`\n"
#~ "    if changed == []:\n"
#~ "        # page is up to date at the commit-SHA level\n"
#~ "        continue\n"
#~ "    add P to candidates\n"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "moved := code_sync.moved_entities(prev, HEAD)\n"
#~ "for each entity_id in moved:\n"
#~ "    for each page P in reverse_index[entity_id]:\n"
#~ "        add P to candidates\n"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "for each page P in content/**/*.md:\n"
#~ "    for each link L in outgoing_links(P):\n"
#~ "        if not resolves_at(HEAD, L):\n"
#~ "            add P to candidates\n"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "repo-map.md       {L-git, L-entity, L-link}   suggest L1 (regenerate from git ls-files)\n"
#~ "data-and-api.md   {L-git, L-entity, L-link}   suggest L2 (body cites moved entities)\n"
#~ "runbook.md        {L-git}                     suggest L1 (commit drift only)\n"
#~ msgstr ""
